``` Microsoft Defender detections for triage (surfaced the blocked Mimikatz / T1003.001 attempt in this lab)
    Data: Defender Operational log, Event ID 1116 (threat detected) / 1117 (action taken)
    ThreatName and Severity are not extracted as fields without a Defender add-on, so rex pulls them from the raw event.
    Defender writes Severity as localized text (Polish and English both appear in this lab), so it is normalized.
    The unpacked Atomic Red Team folder (\AtomicRedTeam\tmp) is excluded: Defender flags the test files on disk. ```
index=endpoint sourcetype="WinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Windows Defender/Operational" (EventCode=1116 OR EventCode=1117)
| rex field=_raw "Name:\s+(?<ThreatName>[^\r\n]+)"
| rex field=_raw "Severity:\s+(?<Severity>[^\r\n]+)"
| eval severity_norm=case(Severity IN ("Severe","Poważny","High","Wysoki"),"high", 1=1,lower(Severity))
| search NOT Path="*AtomicRedTeam\\tmp*"
| table _time host EventCode ThreatName severity_norm Category Action Path
| sort _time desc
